<header><p class="st-kicker">other · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Neutral Moresnet</h1><p class="st-meta">1816 CE – 1920 CE · capital Kelmis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A tiny wedge-shaped territory between Belgium and Prussia, left jointly governed for a century because neither side would give up its zinc mine.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After 1815, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> could not agree on the border near <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-aachen">Aachen</a> because both wanted the valuable <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vieille-montagne">Vieille Montagne</a> zinc mine at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kelmis">Kelmis</a>. In 1816 they left a small triangle of land under joint administration, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-belgium">Belgium</a> taking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> role after 1830.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Neutral Moresnet was run by a mayor and two royal commissioners, one from each neighbour. Its residents paid low taxes and avoided conscription, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vieille-montagne">Vieille Montagne</a> company dominated the economy. After the mine was exhausted in 1885, enthusiasts promoted it as a possible <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esperanto">Esperanto</a> state called Amikejo, and the territory became known for its gambling and distillery.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a> of 1919 assigned the territory to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-belgium">Kingdom of Belgium</a>, effective in 1920. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kelmis">Kelmis</a>, its main village, is now part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium's</a> German-speaking community.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/neutral-moresnet.jpg" alt="Neutral Moresnet" width="320" height="216"><figcaption>Image: ThrashedParanoid · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Moresnet.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1816 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kelmis</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German and French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Moresnet</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1868&amp;focus=neutral-moresnet" aria-label="Neutral Moresnet on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4817 417 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Neutral Moresnet lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5137 673L5099 670"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5099 670h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5137 673h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5137 673h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kelmis. <a href="/atlas?year=1868&amp;focus=neutral-moresnet">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
